Name: http_allow_0rtt
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 0
Last-Modified: 3.13.8

Whether to accept TLS 1.3 early data (0-RTT) on HTTPS connections, so a
client resuming an earlier session can send its first requests without
waiting a round trip for the handshake.

Early data can be replayed, so each session can then be resumed only once
(TLS 1.2 clients included), and an early request with an unsafe method,
such as PUT, POST or DELETE, is answered with 425 Too Early (RFC 8470)
for the client to repeat after the handshake.

Only affects httpd services started with -s, and needs a nonzero
tls_session_timeout.

Every full handshake then stores its session in the TLS session database,
so on a busy server keep tls_sessions_db_path on fast storage such as
tmpfs, or use a tls_sessions_db backend that doesn't sync each write,
such as twom (twoskip, the default, syncs every one).
